messages:
angela: Hey team :wave: I've started a small PR to consolidate the throttle troubleshooting snippets into a compact triage section. Goals: unify SDK examples, add quick checks for context-trimming vs client-side retries, and fix two broken links in the error-ref. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4823

sam: Nice — can you paste the JS backoff snippet here? I'll adapt for Python and Go.

angela: JS backoff I'm proposing:
```
async function callWithBackoff(req) {
  let delay = 300;
  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    const res = await redwood.generate(req);
    if (res.status !== 429) return res;
    await sleep(delay);
    // exponential backoff
    delay *= 2;
  }
  throw new Error('rate-limited');
}
```
Note: add jitter in the final docs and prefer using `Retry-After` when present.

maria: For the docs page we should include header-sniffing example too (pseudo):
```
if (res.headers['retry-after']) {
  delay = parseInt(res.headers['retry-after'], 10) * 1000;
}
```
Also adding a small note about respecting server pacing vs aggressive client retries.

jack: QA question — are we telling customers to trim context or to fallback to a smaller model/shorter context length? We need a tiny decision matrix in the triage doc.

angela: Good call. I added a compact matrix in the PR description:
- If prompt tokens >> model window: prefer prompt trim + user-facing message.
- If tail latency spikes under high concurrency: prefer routing to a cheaper dedicated pool or smaller model variant.
- If intermittent 429 spikes: use client retry with `Retry-After` and exponential backoff + jitter.

sam: I'll open a matching SDK-snippets PR (redwood-js, redwood-py, redwood-go) that mirrors the JS logic and shows header-respect code. Can you add the snippet paths to the docs PR description so reviewers can find them?

angela: Done — added `/snippets/triage/429-backoff-js.md`, `/snippets/triage/429-backoff-py.md`, `/snippets/triage/429-backoff-go.md` to the PR body and linked the err-ref anchor. Fixed two links in the error-ref: `context-window` -> `context-limits` and a broken anchor on the retries section.

qa-bot: Reminder: run the snippet linter before merging: `yarn docs:snippets:lint` and then `yarn docs:build --quiet` to catch rendering/anchor issues.

maria: I also added a brief UX note about showing "estimated remaining tokens" in the console and a pointer to metrics for token consumption. That helps guide whether to trim or fallback.

jack: I'll run a smoke test tomorrow: simulate concurrent small requests (10k) and confirm fallback routing logs include the chosen variant and that the err-ref wording matches observed behavior. I'll post results here.

angela: Thanks all — target is to merge EOD tomorrow if no blockers. @sam I'll DM you the naming map for the SDK snippets so we stay consistent. :thumbsup:
